# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Ammonium cation NH4+: N-H 1.032 A, tetrahedral; charge +1.
# Geometry: typical crystal value (Angstrom converted at 1 A = 1.8897261 Bohr); the experimental geometry, not this
# solver's minimum (LSDA on a grid relaxes it slightly: press Relax to see where).
# A 12 Bohr box at h = 0.15 (the app's default grid) under the default ionic potential.
grid 81 0.15
charge 1
ionic accepted
nucleus 7 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 1 1.1259 1.1259 1.1259
nucleus 1 1.1259 -1.1259 -1.1259
nucleus 1 -1.1259 1.1259 -1.1259
nucleus 1 -1.1259 -1.1259 1.1259
